Model Approval
Who approves a model?
Business stakeholder approval, Model Architect, Security approval
Approval criteria:
Model performance meets defined thresholds
Model evaluation metrics reviewed and acceptable
Rollback plan documented
Code/Pipeline Release Approval
Who approves code/pipeline release for production?
Minimum two peer reviews from ML Engineers/MLOps
Architecture review for infrastructure changes
Security approval for new dependencies or permissions
Approval gates in GitHub Actions:
Automated tests must pass
Security scans must pass (no critical/high vulnerabilities)
Manual approval required before production deployment
ECR Image Approval
Who approves ECR images for production?
Security team review of scan results
Image requirements:
Pass Aqua security scan (no critical/high vulnerabilities)
Immutable tags linked to Git commit SHA
Base images from approved registry only
Resource Restrictions
Instance type restrictions:
Approved instance types defined per workload (retraining vs inference)
Cost optimization through instance type governance
Auto-approval for standard instance types, manual approval for expensive instances
Resource tagging:
Enforce tagging on all resources: Environment, CostCenter, Owner, Project, Workload
Tag compliance monitoring via AWS Config
Automated remediation for untagged resources (alert + potential shutdown)
Additional Governance Controls
Retraining does not auto-deploy: Manual approval gate prevents automatic production deployment
Audit logging: All actions logged to CloudTrail and reviewed regularly
Change management: All production changes follow defined change management process
Disaster recovery: RPO/RTO defined, backup/restore procedures tested regularly (NOT IN SCOPE IN FIRST PHASE)










